im_remesh: make the Instant Meshes core give the same bits on every platform.

Applies to github.com/wjakob/instant-meshes at commit 7b3160864a2e1025af498c84cfed91cbfb613698 (the copy in
third_party/instant-meshes/, which stays unmodified). CMakeLists.txt copies the upstream sources into the build
directory and applies this file there (patch -p1, or git apply).

The changes are modifications of BSD 3-clause code (licenses/instant-meshes-LICENSE.txt), made by the im_remesh
authors in November 2026 and recorded in THIRD_PARTY.md. The changed lines are offered under the same BSD 3-clause
terms as the files they change, so each patched file stays under one licence. They do not change what the algorithm
does, only which of several equally valid results it picks:

  1. std::sort -> std::stable_sort where equal keys can occur (hierarchy.cpp, extract.cpp, bvh.cpp). The order
     std::sort leaves equal keys in differs between libc++, libstdc++ and the MSVC STL.
  2. std::cos / sin / exp / atan2 / acos -> imdet:: versions from src/serial_shim/im_portable_math.h (common.h pulls
     the header in). The C library versions differ in the last bit between macOS, glibc and the MSVC runtime.
  3. reorder.cpp: std::unordered_set -> std::set for the set of unprocessed faces, whose begin() picks the next
     seed face. The iteration order of std::unordered_set differs between standard libraries.

Not touched because the binding never reaches them: smoothcurve.cpp (std::priority_queue), BVH::findKNearest
(std::make_heap / push_heap), generate_graph_coloring (only uint32_t keys are sorted there, no ties to order).

